      "side": 1,
      "message": "This retry path also runs for plain IBV now, but after allocating the missing chain segments it only advances `rxq-\u003etail`; it never constructs or submits the corresponding receive WRs. After buffer-pool exhaustion—or a partial `ibv_post_wq_recv()` failure—the software ring can therefore advance past unposted entries, causing later completions to be matched with the wrong buffers. Could we retain the DV-only behavior here and add an IBV retry path that explicitly posts the recovered chains and handles partial posting correctly?",
